+        "## 14. FAQ — ready answers\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Why does my attack not hit?** Check: a hitbox (flag 2) exists in the frames where the attack should connect; its `$OPT` `d1` is a valid reaction code (≤ 249) — and a character-slot code (30–49) points to a **non-empty** slot; the defender's hurtbox (flag 1) overlaps (use `HITBOX` and `POS`); `GOLPE SET` options are not hiding the hit (e.g. \"ground only\" only affects projectiles).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Why does the projectile not appear?** Flag 0 hit exists in a frame that plays; `PROJETIL_ANIM_NORMAL/ABAIXO/ACIMA` for the current height difference is non-zero and the ANO exists and is non-empty; already 8 projectiles alive; the move missed/was sequence-blocked (see warnings); a projectile ANO has links with links (ignored). The app shows a warning with the reason.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Why does a frame never end?** It has no `$TIME`.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Why does the character not keep moving in the next frame?** The next frame needs `$WACTFLAG: 64` (keep speed) and acceleration must be rewritten.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**How do I change how far the opponent flies?** In the reaction (`EDITAR REAÇÃO`): steps' speeds (unit 0.1 px/tick), durations, and whether ground or air columns apply (opponent height). Use the other reaction group for different hitstop/knockback (5.4).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Where do I save?** Section 13: recommended `Salvar em pasta separada` → `Tap Battle/TBRE/Chars/charNN/`.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**I added/deleted a character folder or replaced a `.txt` and the app does not show it.** Tap `↻` in the title bar (confirm). It rereads the character folders, effects, scenes and sounds and keeps the same character/move if they still exist. Unsaved edits are lost, so `SALVAR` first.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**How do I undo?** `DESFAZER`/`↶`. Saved files keep what was saved; backups are in `Tap Battle/TBRE/Backups/`.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Can you make me a sprite/sound?** No. Tell me what is needed (size, frames, names); the user imports them (11.5).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**What are the numbers 0, 3, 6 of moves?** Special move slots; they can only be transplanted onto 0, 3 and 6.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**The app says \"recorte fora do PNG\".** A `$SPR_n` rectangle is outside its sheet: fix `$x/$y/$w/$h` (remember characters use 2× physical pixels in the `.cnv.txt`).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**What does an amber vs. red warning mean?** Red = the game would close or fail; amber = the editor sees something the game handles differently.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "## 15. Engine internals — answers to the questions an AI asked about the combat system\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "This section answers, in one place, the detailed questions a modding AI asked about how *Tap Battle* really executes attacks (flow, files, collision, damage, reactions, physics, projectiles, animation, effects, flags, internal methods, examples, validation). It was written by reading the game source (`TCBManajer.java`, 33 318 lines; \"jogo:N\" = line N) and by comparing it with the app's simulator (`BattleSim`). **Where the in-app help (section 5/6/Appendix A) and this section differ, this section (confirmed in the code) wins.**\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Scope guard.** This section is background so that *you* understand what the user describes and can write correct `.txt` content in Mode B. It is **not** material to teach: never turn it into instructions to edit the binaries (`000.dac/.bin/.cnv`) or to use `▲ DADOS / EDITAR`. When the user asks how to do something in the app, answer with the app's functions (Mode A).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Confidence tags used on every claim.** **[CODE]** verified in the game code (line given when useful). **[DOC]** stated by the app's documentation but not re-verified here. **[INFERRED]** deduced from data or usage. **[UNKNOWN]** could not be determined from the code (tell the user instead of guessing).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Method names are the decompiled ones** (`var2` etc. are decompiler names; tables are `ChrGameData[player+3]` for a character's pac and `pGameData` for `gamedata.pac`). `md N` is the state/task number passed to `Game(gw, md)`; a fighter or object is a task (`TCB`) whose `md` selects what runs each tick.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**A correction of the app's older help text (confirmed in the code).** `PROJETIL_ANIM_ABAIXO` is used when the **attacker** is ≥ 51 px lower than the opponent (`PlayerYPos[att] >= PlayerYPos[opp] + 3342336`), `PROJETIL_ANIM_ACIMA` when the attacker is ≥ 37 px higher, `PROJETIL_ANIM_NORMAL` in between. Older UI/help text said \"opponent far below/above\", which is the opposite reading.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.1 Flow of an attack, from the command to the end (questions 1–8)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "Tags: **[CODE]** verified in `TCBManajer.java` (line = `jogo:N`), **[INFERRED]**, **[UNKNOWN]**. Everything is driven by `TCBManajer.Run` (jogo:29937), called once per rendered GL frame by `AndroidGLRender.onDrawFrame`; there is **no fixed timestep**, the logic runs one tick per frame **[CODE]**.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "1. **Pad task md 38** (jogo:25907; md 37 only initialises the pads) reads the virtual pad/touches into `JoyTrig/Joy`, `TouchesCommand`, `_commandButton` through a 3-slot lockstep buffer (`BTDataSet`/`BTSend`/`BTRev`, jogo:1613/1377) **even offline** — a few ticks of input latency **[INFERRED]**.\n" +
+        "2. **Input task md 946** (jogo:23730, one per player, prio 13056+p) runs only if `bGameStart && iBackXOffset == 0 && iEventStatus == 0` (jogo:23733). Pad mode: `PlayerKey[p] = Joy`, direction history in `KeyBuf[p][0..3]/KeyBufTime`, `Dash`, `TameCnt` (charge), `Footwork`. Touch mode (`iControlType[p] == 2`): `switch (TouchesCommand)` (jogo:23775); case 1 spawns an AI macro task md 947 (prio 13184+p+2, `_work[5] = _commandButton`) and sets `AICtrl[p] = true`.\n" +
+        "3. **Touch macro md 947 → 948 → 953-960** (jogo:23969-24442): `CPUSeqNo` selects a row of HDAT 6 of `ChrGameData[p+3]` (pairs *(command+1, frame count)*, next sequence at byte 8, end flag at byte 9); `SeqKey[command]` (jogo:584) is turned into `PlayerKey/JoyTrig`.\n" +
+        "4. **Fighter task md 863/864/872…** (created by `CreatePlayer`, prio 13569+p, jogo:3354). Idle md 872 (jogo:20874) calls `CommonNormal(gw, allowMove, _, allowDash, autoFace, allowAttack)` (jogo:2747). `CommonNormal` calls `CmdCheck(gw, p)` (jogo:2404; returns a code 0–23) and ORs `PlayerAttackFlag[p] |= 1 << code` (jogo:2782).\n" +
+        "5. **Command code → `SpecialType` (= the HDAT 4 row = the move number `GOLPE_n`)** inside `CommonNormal` (jogo:3015-3114) **[CODE]**:\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "| `CmdCheck` code | Meaning (inferred from use) | Result |\n" +
+        "|---|---|---|\n" +
+        "| 1 | special 1 | `SpecialType` **0** on the ground / **3** jumping or falling / **6** flying (`PlayerAir`) |\n" +
+        "| 2 | special 2 | **1** / **4** / **7** |\n" +
+        "| 3 | special 3 | **2** / **5** / **8** |\n" +
+        "| 4 | rage activation | **14** (ground) / **15** (flying) |\n" +
+        "| 23 | alternate rage | **16** on the ground (`PlayerYPos == 15728640`) else **17** |\n" +
+        "| 6, 7 | evade | `SpecialType` 18/19, md 880 → md 865 (vanish/reappear, ANO 87/88); **no HDAT 4 attack is started** |\n" +
+        "| 8 | ultimate | **9** (ground/flying) / **10** (jump), md 923 |\n" +
+        "| 9 | super ultimate | **11** / **12** |\n" +
+        "| 5 | charge | md 901 |\n" +
+        "| 11, 12, 13, 17 | normals | **hard-coded ANO 29–39** (md 878/886); they do **not** use HDAT 4 and need `PlayerAttack[p] == 0` |\n" +
+        "| 15, 16 | dash | md 891 (ANO 6–9, 82/83) |\n" +
+        "| 18, 19 | evade dash | md 897 (ANO 2/3) |\n" +
+        "| 22 | sealed art | md 894; `PlayerArtsSeal` is declared (jogo:122) but never written, so 22 is unreachable in practice |\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "   `PlayerAttackFlag` is only a \"command seen\" bitmask read by `MissionClearCheck` (tutorial); it has **no gameplay effect**. The **move number in the editor (`GOLPE_0…`) is this `SpecialType`**; moves 0/3/6 are the \"special 1\" slots (ground/air/flying).\n" +
+        "6. **Special start md 880** (jogo:21699): `SYNCHRO_DEC(100)` if the current ANO is 40–88; clears `TameCnt`/`PlayerKey`; calls **`StartPlayerAttack`** (jogo:31614-31674); then md 881 → 882. Ultimates go md 923 → 926 → 927 → 928 → 881. `StartPlayerAttack` **[CODE]**: clears `wFlag` bits 1 and 4096, `_SetObj(150+4p)`, sets `PlayerAttack = 1`, `PlayerHitStop = 10`, `DamageHitBack = 0`, `GuardHitBack = 13`, `CancelTime = 0`, `DamageHitActNo[opp] = 0`, `SpecialBulletNumber = 0`; reads the HDAT 4 row `SpecialType` (next section): `SpecialKind[p]` (= ATK_FLAGS), `ANIM_INICIAL`, `BulletAction[p][0..1]`; `AngryOn = true` for SpecialType 14/15; if the current ANO is 40–92 (not 80/89) and the new ANIM_INICIAL ≥ 40 and SpecialType not 9–12 it spawns a chain flash (md 965, effect ANO 8); it sets `objExec.ano = 0` then `_SetAct(acttype, ANIM_INICIAL)` (jogo:31661-31662) — the `ano = 0` makes the same ANO restart.\n" +
