+        "**Other tables used by attacks [CODE].** HDAT 3 (body data, row 0): byte 0/1 forward/back speed, byte 3 body width (half used for walls), byte 4 `PlayerYLimit`, byte 5 grab distance, byte 6 `AirType`/\"can fly\", byte 7 dash speed, byte 10 charge gain, byte 12/14 attack/defense base, **byte 13 clash reaction** (the reaction a hitbox with `ATK_FLAGS` bit 2 forces on the opponent), byte 16 sealed-art ANO. HDAT 13: cutscene rows (stride `2*XSize[13]` bytes). HDAT 14–33 (character) / 10–39 (gamedata): reactions, 14 columns (15.5). HDAT 6: CPU sequences. HDAT 5: score and combo-scaling table. HDAT 37/35: rage multiplier and event damage.\n" +
