+        "- **A pattern that never hits**: P1 keeps testing for its 3 ticks; nothing happens; `CancelTime` stays 0 (no cancel on whiff).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**B. A projectile that hits once.** Move row with `PROJETIL_ANIM_NORMAL = 21`; the cast ANO has a type-0 entry in its pattern (x = 30, y = −40). `PlayerTail` spawns md 970 (`BulletNum` 1) → md 971: the ANO 21 script moves it each tick; its pattern with a type-2 box and `$OPT` (d0 damage, d1 reaction) is armed (`iHitCount = 1`); md 935 detects overlap with the defender's hurtbox via `tcbReqHit` → `DamageChange` with the **owner's** stats; defender hit-stop full, projectile half; if `SpecialType` matches, the owner gets `CancelTime = 20`, `wFlag |= 4096`; the projectile then switches to `PROJETIL_ANIM_AO_ACERTAR`/global ANO or dies (unless `ATK_FLAGS & 1`).\n" +
+        "**Multi-hit**: either several consecutive patterns each with a hit block (each re-arms `iHitCount`), or a projectile ANO built the same way; every hit uses full formula with growing combo scaling.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**C. What to edit in a move such as `GOLPE_9` (cast ANO 51, projectile ANO 49, impact ANO 50)** — first read the `$GOLPE_9` text to see which fields point to 49/50/51 (15.7). Only damage: `$OPT` `d0` in the projectile's hit patterns. Only reaction: `d1`. Projectile speed: `$XSPEED` of the projectile ANO. Number of hits: patterns with a type-2 box. Impact animation: `PROJETIL_ANIM_AO_ACERTAR` or `_GLOBAL` ANO contents (or change which ANO they point to). Appearance vs. collision: sprites/`$IMG`/`$MID`/RAZ/`$MOVE` = appearance; type-2/1 boxes and `$OPT` = collision/damage.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**D. Validation tests for an external implementation (compare numbers, not feelings).**\n" +
+        "1. *Formula*: `AttackMul=100, DeffenceMul=0, d0=10` → 10; `d0=1` → 2 (minimum 2); flag 28 with `d0=1` → 1; ANO 92 → 0; `d0=0` → 0.\n" +
+        "2. *Combo scaling*: same hit repeated: `idx` sequence 0,1,0,1,2,3…13 (c = 0,1,2,3,4…) using the data table; value ≥ 1.\n" +
+        "3. *Hit once*: a 10-tick pattern with a hitbox deals damage exactly once; two consecutive patterns with hit blocks deal it twice.\n" +
+        "4. *Strict overlap*: boxes touching at an edge (right of A == left of B) → no hit; 1 px overlap → hit; flipped facing mirrors X.\n" +
+        "5. *Hit-stop*: both fighters frozen for `PlayerHitStop` ticks (10 specials, 6 basics); group 3 half for body hits; group 4 none.\n" +
+        "6. *Reaction rows*: row duration `max(dur,1)` ticks; `-1` keeps, `-2` halves (raw unsigned quirk); speed unit 1 = 0.1 px/tick; X friction zeroes speed when the sign flips; 255 = hold until `DamageTime ≥ 255` then type 2; COMP 11 knocks down on landing; WALL 2/3 restarts at COMP on wall/landing.\n" +
+        "7. *Order*: reaction accelerates-then-moves, animation script moves-then-accelerates; load tick of an animation pattern moves nothing; accel is zeroed on load; speed zeroed unless `wActFlag & 64`.\n" +
+        "8. *Limits*: 10 boxes/frame, 13 links, 255 patterns, `time ≤ 255`, OPT1 ≤ 249, BulletNum < 8.\n" +
+        "9. *Trade*: both hit in the same tick → OPT1 forced to 0, index 1 wins double KO.\n" +
+        "10. *KO*: life ≤ 0 → type 2 regardless of OPT1, then lying (ANO 24).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**E. What cannot be reproduced from the extracted data alone [CODE/UNKNOWN].** The numeric content of the data pacs (gamedata reaction rows, combo-scaling table HDAT 5, `HDAT3[13]` clash reactions, card/level stats), the CPU decision code (random guard, AI macros), the lockstep input buffer latency, exact screen/camera scrolling (`md 19`), and the cutscene events (HDAT 13). Everything else in combat is deterministic integer logic that the app's `BattleSim` already mirrors.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.13 Where to read next, and what is still unknown (questions 93–97)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Study order in `TCBManajer.java` [CODE]:** `Run` (29937) → `Game` dispatch (4755) → `CommonNormal` (2747) + `CmdCheck` (2404) → `StartPlayerAttack` (31614) → md 882/883 (21735, 21950) → `PlayerTail` (29714) → `_ActReqMain` (31772) → `CheckOptFlag` (2112) → `CheckObjHit` (2045) → md 935 (23194) → `DamageChange` (3466) → md 876/877 (20983, 21259) → `DamageEnd` (4043) / `AttackEnd` (901) → md 970/971 (24534-24698) → md 996 (25096) → md 19 (15114). The app's `BattleSim` mirrors these (its comments cite `jogo:N`, but **some older citations in the app source point to the wrong lines**; trust the lines in this file).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Tables available:** this file (15.1–15.12), Appendix A (the app's own help), `GameRules` limits (section 7), HDAT 4 (5.5, 15.2), reactions (5.4, 15.5), flags (5.2, 15.10).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Open / unconfirmed [UNKNOWN]:** triggers of md 898, 909, 921; meaning of `wOptFlag` 256 and of WACTFLAG 512/1024/2048; HDAT 4 bytes 44/46; whether `tcb.skip` is ever set; md 998–1122; the gamedata/combo-scaling/clash-reaction **values** (in the pacs); the exact units of `AttackMul/DeffenceMul` (percentages inferred); whether the `HOMING == 0` inversion is intended; `ThrowDamage` paths (dead in this build).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Details easy to miss [CODE]:** the game runs one tick per rendered frame; the same `ano`+`acttype` passed to `_SetAct` is ignored (set `ano = 0` first); a hitbox frame without `$OPT` has damage 0 and reaction 0; OPT1 ≥ 250 and > 10 boxes crash the game; ANO numbers are local to each character's DAC; `-2` speed in reactions is read raw/unsigned; `SetLoad` does not re-read an already loaded pac id.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "",
+    };
+}
diff -ruN a/AiHelpShare.java b/AiHelpShare.java
--- a/AiHelpShare.java	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/AiHelpShare.java	2026-10-24 22:23:41.569032233 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+package com.zue.attackeditor;
+
+import android.app.Activity;
+import android.content.ClipData;
+import android.content.Intent;
+import android.media.MediaScannerConnection;
+import android.net.Uri;
+import android.os.Environment;
+import android.widget.Toast;
+import java.io.File;
+import java.io.FileOutputStream;
+import java.io.OutputStreamWriter;
+import java.io.Writer;
+
+/**
+ * Botao "Ajuda de IA": gera o TBRHelp.md ({@link AiHelp}), grava em Download/ e abre o compartilhamento do Android para o usuario mandar o arquivo a uma IA.
+ * O app ja tem acesso a todos os arquivos; o content:// vem do indexador de midia (nao precisa de FileProvider nem de manifest).
+ */
+final class AiHelpShare {
+    private AiHelpShare() { }
+
+    /** Versao do app, so informativa dentro do arquivo. */
+    static final String BUILD = "java_novo2-34";
+
+    static File target() {
+        return new File(Environment.getExternalStoragePublicDirectory(Environment.DIRECTORY_DOWNLOADS), AiHelp.FILE_NAME);
+    }
+
+    static void run(final Activity a) {
+        final BusyDialog bd = BusyDialog.show(a, "Criando " + AiHelp.FILE_NAME);
+        new Thread(new Runnable() {
+            @Override public void run() {
+                try {
+                    bd.set("Montando o documento…", 0, 3);
+                    String doc = AiHelp.build(BUILD);
+                    bd.set("Gravando em Download/…", 1, 3);
+                    final File f = target();
+                    File dir = f.getParentFile();
+                    if (dir != null && !dir.isDirectory() && !dir.mkdirs()) throw new java.io.IOException("não foi possível criar " + dir.getPath());
+                    Writer w = new OutputStreamWriter(new FileOutputStream(f), "UTF-8");
+                    try { w.write(doc); } finally { w.close(); }
+                    bd.set("Preparando o compartilhamento…", 2, 3);
+                    MediaScannerConnection.scanFile(a, new String[]{f.getPath()}, new String[]{"text/markdown"}, new MediaScannerConnection.OnScanCompletedListener() {
+                        @Override public void onScanCompleted(final String path, final Uri uri) {
+                            a.runOnUiThread(new Runnable() { @Override public void run() { bd.dismiss(); share(a, f, uri); } });
+                        }
+                    });
+                } catch (final Exception e) {
+                    a.runOnUiThread(new Runnable() { @Override public void run() {
+                        bd.dismiss();
+                        new I18nBuilder(a).setTitle("Ajuda de IA")
+                                .setMessage("Não foi possível criar o " + AiHelp.FILE_NAME + " em Download/: " + e.getMessage()
+                                        + "\n\nConfira se o app tem \"Acesso a todos os arquivos\" (Configurações do Android > Apps > Attack Editor > Permissões).")
+                                .setPositiveButton("OK", null).show();
+                    } });
+                }
+            }
+        }, "ai-help").start();
+    }
+
+    private static void share(Activity a, File f, Uri uri) {
+        if (uri == null) {
+            I18nUi.toast(a, AiHelp.FILE_NAME + " criado em Download/, mas o Android não liberou o compartilhamento. Envie o arquivo pelo gerenciador de arquivos.", Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show();
+            return;
+        }
+        Intent send = new Intent(Intent.ACTION_SEND);
+        send.setType("text/plain");
+        send.putExtra(Intent.EXTRA_STREAM, uri);
+        send.putExtra(Intent.EXTRA_SUBJECT, AiHelp.FILE_NAME);
+        send.putExtra(Intent.EXTRA_TEXT, AiHelp.shareMessage());
+        send.setClipData(ClipData.newRawUri(AiHelp.FILE_NAME, uri));
+        send.addFlags(Intent.FLAG_GRANT_READ_URI_PERMISSION);
+        try {
+            a.startActivity(Intent.createChooser(send, AiHelp.chooserTitle()));
+            I18nUi.toast(a, AiHelp.FILE_NAME + " salvo em Download/ (" + f.length() / 1024 + " KB)", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show();
+        } catch (Exception e) {
+            I18nUi.toast(a, AiHelp.FILE_NAME + " criado em Download/. Não achei app para compartilhar: " + e.getMessage(), Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show();
+        }
+    }
+}
